---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import {CHECKED,SOURCES,RECORDS,TOPICS,FAQ} from '../data/tax-guide.mjs';
import '../styles/tax-guide.css';
---
<Base title="Your tax return. One clear step at a time." description="A free Australian employee tax-return preparation guide. Check your records, understand work-expense rules and follow the steps to lodge yourself in myTax.">
<header class="hl-wrap tax-simple-head"><div class="hl-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Tax return guide</div><span class="hl-eyebrow">FREE · AUSTRALIAN EMPLOYEE TAX GUIDE</span><h1>Less tax-time guesswork.</h1><p>Organise your work expenses. See what still needs checking.<br/>Take a clear checklist into your own myTax return.</p><div class="tax-badges"><span>No sign-up</span><span>Your entries stay here</span><span>Free to use</span></div></header>
<section class="hl-wrap tax-workspace" id="tax-companion" aria-label="Tax return companion">
<aside class="tax-sidebar"><span class="hl-eyebrow">YOUR TAX-TIME COMPANION</span><h2>Small steps.<br/>Clear progress.</h2><ol id="tax-progress"><li aria-current="step"><span>01</span>Your starting point</li><li><span>02</span>Your work</li><li><span>03</span>Gather your records</li><li><span>04</span>Explore expense topics</li><li><span>05</span>Your myTax checklist</li></ol><p>Answers stay in this page’s memory. Download your checklist before leaving. We do not request documents or account details.</p><button type="button" class="tax-text-button" id="tax-reset">Start over</button></aside>
<div class="tax-main"><div class="tax-step-meta"><span id="tax-step-count">STEP 1 OF 5</span><span>Guided checklist</span></div><div class="tax-track"><div id="tax-track-fill"></div></div>
<form id="tax-form" novalidate>
<section data-tax-step="0"><div class="tax-coach"><span class="tax-coach-mark" aria-hidden="true">h.</span><p>Let’s start with the basics. Which year and income types are you preparing?</p></div><h2 tabindex="-1">Your starting point</h2><label class="tax-label" for="tax-year">Income year</label><select id="tax-year" name="year" required><option value="">Choose an income year</option><option value="2025-26">2025–26 · 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2026</option><option value="2024-25">2024–25 · 1 July 2024 to 30 June 2025</option><option value="future">2026–27 · still in progress</option><option value="other">An earlier year</option></select>
<fieldset><legend>Have you established your Australian tax residency?</legend><label class="tax-choice"><input type="radio" name="residency" value="resident"/><span>I am an Australian resident for tax purposes for the full year, aged 18 or over.</span></label><label class="tax-choice"><input type="radio" name="residency" value="other"/><span>Part-year or foreign resident, working holiday maker, or under 18.</span></label><label class="tax-choice"><input type="radio" name="residency" value="unsure"/><span>I am not sure yet.</span></label><small>Tax residency is different from citizenship or visa status. <a href={SOURCES.residency.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check the ATO residency guidance ↗</a></small></fieldset>
<fieldset><legend>What does your return include?</legend><label class="tax-choice"><input type="radio" name="income" value="simple"/><span>Australian employee wages, possibly Australian bank interest, and ordinary work expenses.</span></label><label class="tax-choice"><input type="radio" name="income" value="complex"/><span>Other matters, such as business or ABN income, rental property, shares, crypto, foreign income or capital gains.</span></label><label class="tax-choice"><input type="radio" name="income" value="unsure"/><span>I am not sure, or my return has other items.</span></label></fieldset><div id="tax-coverage" class="tax-notice" hidden role="status"></div><p id="tax-outside-links" hidden><a href={SOURCES.lodge.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Continue with ATO self-lodgment guidance ↗</a> · <a href={SOURCES.help.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Get help from the ATO ↗</a></p></section>
<section data-tax-step="1" hidden><div class="tax-coach"><span class="tax-coach-mark" aria-hidden="true">h.</span><p>We’ll point you to the occupation guide closest to your work. Your job title alone never establishes a deduction.</p></div><h2 tabindex="-1">What kind of work do you do?</h2><fieldset><legend class="tax-sr">Choose your work</legend><label class="tax-choice"><input type="radio" name="job" value="retail"/><span><strong>Retail</strong><small>Shops, supermarkets and sales teams</small></span></label><label class="tax-choice"><input type="radio" name="job" value="hospitality"/><span><strong>Café, restaurant & hospitality</strong><small>Baristas, waitstaff and hospitality employees</small></span></label><label class="tax-choice"><input type="radio" name="job" value="other"/><span><strong>Another employee role</strong><small>Use the general employee guidance</small></span></label></fieldset><p class="tax-muted">If you have more than one role, review the relevant ATO guidance for each. This first version does not cover sole traders or businesses.</p></section>
<section data-tax-step="2" hidden><div class="tax-coach"><span class="tax-coach-mark" aria-hidden="true">h.</span><p>A good return starts with good records. Tick a group when you have reviewed it; leave anything unfinished unchecked.</p></div><h2 tabindex="-1">Gather the essentials.</h2><div class="tax-records">{RECORDS.map(r=><div class="tax-record"><label><input type="checkbox" name="records" value={r.id}/><strong>{r.title}</strong></label><p>{r.detail}</p><a href={SOURCES[r.source].url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the ATO guidance ↗</a></div>)}</div><p class="tax-note">You can continue with unfinished items. Your download will show what still needs checking.</p></section>
<section data-tax-step="3" hidden><div class="tax-coach"><span class="tax-coach-mark" aria-hidden="true">h.</span><p>Add expenses you want to organise, then read the rules for their categories. You can also browse topics without entering amounts.</p></div><h2 tabindex="-1">Your work expenses, organised.</h2><p id="tax-job-source"></p><section class="tax-expense-tool" aria-label="Expense organiser"><h3>Put your expenses in one place.</h3><p>Enter what you paid and your documented work use. We do the arithmetic and keep the details together.</p><div class="tax-entry-grid"><div><label for="expense-category">Expense topic</label><select id="expense-category">{TOPICS.map(t=><option value={t.id}>{t.title}</option>)}</select></div><div><label for="expense-date">Date paid</label><input id="expense-date" type="date"/></div><div class="tax-entry-wide"><label for="expense-description">Short description <span>(optional)</span></label><input id="expense-description" type="text" maxlength="100" placeholder="e.g. work phone bill — no personal details"/></div><div><label for="expense-paid">Total cost (AUD)</label><input id="expense-paid" type="number" min="0.01" max="1000000" step="0.01" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="0.00"/></div><div><label for="expense-work">Work use (%)</label><input id="expense-work" type="number" min="0" max="100" step="0.01" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="Based on your records"/></div><div class="tax-entry-wide"><label for="expense-reimbursed">Employer reimbursement for this work use (AUD)</label><input id="expense-reimbursed" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" step="0.01" inputmode="decimal" value="0"/><small>Enter 0 if none. If a payment mixes work and private reimbursement, separate it before adding this entry.</small></div></div><p id="expense-error" role="alert"></p><button id="expense-add" type="button" class="hl-button">Add expense +</button><div class="tax-expense-total"><span>Unreimbursed work-use cost to review</span><strong id="expense-total">$0.00</strong><small>This is not an approved deduction or a refund estimate.</small></div><div id="expense-list" aria-live="polite"></div><details class="tax-arithmetic"><summary>How this total works</summary><p>Cost × your work-use percentage − reimbursement for that work use. Each entry is rounded to cents. For example, a hypothetical $100 bill × 40% work use − $10 reimbursement leaves $30 of cost to review.</p><p>We have not assessed whether a cost is deductible, when it can be claimed, or whether depreciation or other special rules apply. Some recorded expenses may have no deduction. Do not enter this combined total directly into myTax.</p></details></section><h3 class="tax-topic-heading">Read the rules for your topics</h3><div class="tax-topics">{TOPICS.map(t=><article class="tax-topic"><label><input type="checkbox" name="topics" value={t.id}/><strong>{t.title}</strong></label><p>{t.summary}</p><details><summary>Explain this topic</summary><span class="hl-eyebrow">{t.tag}</span><p>{t.explanation}</p><h3>What to gather</h3><p>{t.records}</p><div class="tax-example"><strong>A useful distinction</strong><p>{t.example}</p></div><a href={SOURCES[t.source].url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{SOURCES[t.source].title} ↗</a></details></article>)}</div><p class="tax-note">No relevant expenses? Continue without selecting a topic. Do not invent a claim to fill a category.</p></section>
<section data-tax-step="4" hidden><div class="tax-coach"><span class="tax-coach-mark" aria-hidden="true">h.</span><p>You have a preparation plan. Keep it beside you as you work through the official return.</p></div><h2 tabindex="-1">Your next steps, together.</h2><div class="tax-summary"><span class="hl-eyebrow">YOUR PREPARATION SNAPSHOT</span><h3 id="tax-summary-year"></h3><p id="tax-summary-work"></p><p id="tax-record-count"></p><ul id="tax-pending"></ul><p id="tax-selected-topics"></p><div id="tax-summary-expenses" hidden><span>Unreimbursed work-use cost to review</span><strong id="tax-summary-total"></strong><small>From your entries. Not an approved tax deduction.</small></div></div><h3>Follow along in myTax</h3><ol class="tax-lodge-steps"><li><strong>Open the official service.</strong> Sign in to myGov, select ATO online services and the correct return year. Never enter your login details here.</li><li><strong>Check and personalise.</strong> Review personal details and select all applicable income and deduction sections. Check every employer’s finalised statement and interest; add missing income without duplicating pre-filled amounts.</li><li><strong>Work through the return.</strong> Check the ATO help beside each field and the selected year’s rules. Enter supported amounts; review other relevant sections, including offsets, Medicare, private health insurance and study loans.</li><li><strong>Review, then lodge yourself.</strong> Resolve missing information, review the estimate and read the declaration. Submit in myTax only when satisfied. Keep the receipt and supporting records. An estimate is not the final notice of assessment.</li></ol><p class="tax-note">The wording and arrangement in myTax may change. Follow the current ATO screen instructions. Nothing you do on Howloop submits a return.</p><div class="tax-result-actions"><button type="button" class="hl-button" id="tax-download">Download my checklist ↓</button><button type="button" class="tax-secondary" id="tax-csv" hidden>Download expenses CSV ↓</button><button type="button" class="tax-secondary" id="tax-print">Print / save PDF</button></div><details class="tax-text-export"><summary>View plain-text checklist</summary><pre id="tax-checklist-text"></pre></details><p id="tax-download-status" role="status"></p><div class="tax-official-links"><a href="https://my.gov.au/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open official myGov ↗</a><a href={SOURCES.simulator.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Try the ATO practice simulator ↗</a></div></section>
<p id="tax-error" role="alert"></p><div class="tax-controls"><button type="button" id="tax-back" class="tax-secondary" hidden>← Back</button><button type="submit" id="tax-next" class="hl-button">Continue →</button></div></form><noscript><p>Enable JavaScript to build your checklist. The guidance and official links below are available without it.</p></noscript></div></section>
<section class="hl-wrap tax-reading"><p class="tax-scope-bottom">Howloop provides general education and an expense organiser. It is not a registered tax agent or an ATO service, and cannot approve claims, calculate a refund or lodge your return.</p><div><span class="hl-eyebrow">UNDERSTAND BEFORE YOU ENTER</span><h2>A claim is more<br/>than a number.</h2><p>For every expense, check what you paid, how it relates to earning your income, any private use, employer reimbursements and the evidence you hold. Do not treat a suggested category as a personal entitlement.</p><p>Keep the expense and its explanation together. If you cannot explain a figure, pause and read the ATO guidance before entering it. This companion deliberately leaves claim amounts and refund estimates to the official return.</p><a href={SOURCES.expenses.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the ATO employee expense guide ↗</a></div><div class="tax-faq">{FAQ.map(f=><details><summary>{f.question}</summary><p>{f.answer}</p><a href={SOURCES[f.source].url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{SOURCES[f.source].title} ↗</a></details>)}</div></section>
<section class="hl-wrap tax-ai" id="tax-ai" hidden><span class="hl-eyebrow">OPTIONAL · AI EXPLANATIONS</span><h2>A term still unclear?</h2><p>Ask a general question about one of the topics above. AI explanations can be wrong; check the linked ATO source. This assistant cannot decide your entitlement, calculate a claim or complete a return.</p><p>Enabling this panel loads Cloudflare’s verification service. Sending a question shares it with OpenAI; your checklist is not included.</p><button type="button" class="tax-secondary" id="tax-ai-enable">Enable AI explanations</button><div id="tax-ai-panel" hidden><form id="tax-ai-form"><label for="tax-ai-topic">Topic</label><select id="tax-ai-topic">{TOPICS.map(t=><option value={t.id}>{t.title}</option>)}</select><label for="tax-question">Your general question</label><textarea id="tax-question" maxlength="600" rows="3" placeholder="Why is a normal work dress code different from a uniform?" required></textarea><label class="tax-consent"><input type="checkbox" id="tax-ai-consent" required/><span>I agree to send this question and selected topic to OpenAI through Howloop. I will not include names, TFNs, account details, documents or personal financial figures. <a href="/privacy">Privacy details</a></span></label><div id="tax-turnstile"></div><button class="hl-button" type="submit">Explain this →</button></form><p id="tax-ai-status" role="status"></p><div id="tax-ai-answer" class="tax-notice" hidden></div></div></section>
<section class="hl-wrap tax-sources"><h2>Built around sources you can check.</h2><p>Published and general sources checked {CHECKED}. The year selector labels your checklist; it does not load tax rates or turn this into a complete year-specific tax calculation. Howloop’s guided content is pre-written. Optional AI explanations are labelled separately when available.</p><div>{Object.values(SOURCES).map(s=><a href={s.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{s.title} ↗</a>)}</div><p>Found a confusing step? <a href="mailto:hello@howloop.how">hello@howloop.how</a> · <a href="/editorial-policy">Our publishing standard</a></p></section>
</Base>
<script>import '../scripts/tax-guide';</script>
